policy or executive order.

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:45.950
And Rand Paul would then appear on TV and
he would sort of put like a slightly less

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:48.620
crazy spin on it compared to Donald Trump.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:51.160
And compare it to the way Trump was talking
about the issue.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:54.670
Rand Paul would seem marginally more rational.

00:00:54.670 --> 00:01:00.250
But what's going on now is that with Donald
Trump gone, Rand Paul is still saying equivalently

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:03.100
wacky things as to what he was saying before.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:09.490
But without the even crazier Trump to compare
him to, he seems as out of his mind as he

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:11.420
has been for many, many years.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:13.200
So let's take a look at some of these.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:17.930
Rand Paul here says you can't impeach a president
who has left office, of course, ignoring the

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:21.140
fact that Donald Trump was impeached while
in office.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:23.360
It's the trial that will start soon.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:27.400
But the impeachment of Trump, remember, impeachment
happens in the House, did take place while

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:28.400
Donald Trump was president.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:33.740
He had a vote on the floor and 45 Republicans
said, look, you can't really impeach somebody

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:35.030
who's already left office.

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:36.780
That doesn't make any sense at all.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.830
So they've been repeating this one a lot.

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:39.830
It's wrong.

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:43.200
Trump was impeached while president.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.799
But imagine that defense anywhere else.

00:01:45.799 --> 00:01:47.930
The murder I committed.

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:50.880
Yeah, I did that when I was a manager of a
KFC.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.790
I don't have that job anymore.

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:57.509
So anything I did while working at that job
doesn't count because I can't get fired from

00:01:57.509 --> 00:01:58.509
there anymore.

00:01:58.509 --> 00:01:59.909
I already don't work there.

00:01:59.909 --> 00:02:02.979
What where else would that argument apply?

00:02:02.979 --> 00:02:08.810
And of course, it's factually wrong since
Trump was impeached while he was president

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.780
